00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:45.558
-I saw RM.
-Yeah.

00:03:45.558 --> 00:03:48.795
-And then I thought --
-What did you think of him?

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.095
-He was amazing.

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:51.163
-Oh, thank you.

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:55.201
But, Jungkook --
when I first saw him,

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:57.303
I was only wearing
the underwear.

00:03:57.303 --> 00:04:01.540
-Yeah.
-Wait. What?

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.676
You were only wearing underwear?
-I mean in the house.

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.677
-Yeah.
-In my home.

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:05.845
-What?

00:04:05.845 --> 00:04:07.880
-Yeah, he came like,
"Oh, I'm the new member."

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:11.451
I was, like,
only wearing panties and --

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:14.187
Yeah, that was
the first impression.

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:16.021
-So, who put this together? You?

00:04:16.021 --> 00:04:18.490
-No, I was just, like,
the first member

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:19.625
for this group and --

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:20.693
-You were?
-Yeah.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:21.794
-Number two?
-Yeah.

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:22.862
-Three.
-Three.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:25.130
-Who's three?
-Three.

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.966
-Suga, you came in,
what happened?

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:28.167
How did you hear?

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:50.456
-We were boys.

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:52.524
-Did you ever think BTS
would become this big?

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:53.659
-No.
-Never.

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:55.361
-No.
-Never.

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.363
-When you doubted yourself,
what got you

00:04:57.363 --> 00:05:00.266
to the next level of like,
"Hey, I can do this"?

00:05:16.782 --> 00:05:18.150
Do you remember the
first time you ever performed

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:19.285
in front of a crowd?

00:05:19.285 --> 00:05:21.187
And what was that like?

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:25.424
-It was our debut showcase.

00:05:25.424 --> 00:05:30.229
There were about
200 to 300 people.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:31.731
-300 people.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:33.966
-Now you have
billions of people watching.

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:36.402
But 300 people
meant a lot to you, right?

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:39.438
-Right, of course.
-I still can never forget it.

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:43.643
Everything happened so fast,
and it was overwhelming.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:44.777
-It was.
-Yeah.

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:47.646
-And I cried after the show.

00:05:47.646 --> 00:05:49.048
-You did?
-Yeah.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:51.416
-Everyone cried.
-Yeah.

00:05:51.416 --> 00:05:53.018
-Everyone cried.
-Everyone cried?

00:05:53.018 --> 00:05:55.621
-Yes, yes.
-Yeah, because it's a big thing.

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.756
"Map of the Soul: 7"
is out now.

00:05:57.756 --> 00:05:58.824
Yo!

00:05:58.824 --> 00:05:59.925
-Yo!

00:05:59.925 --> 00:06:02.828
-What is the significance
behind the "7"?

00:06:02.828 --> 00:06:05.364
-You know, it's a
lucky number, of course.

00:06:05.364 --> 00:06:07.833
-Seven members.
-Yeah, seven members.

00:06:07.833 --> 00:06:10.203
It's been seven years
since we've been together.

00:06:10.203 --> 00:06:11.704
-Wow. Seven, seven.
It's good luck.

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:13.105
-Yeah, 7-7-7,
so it's like a jackpot.

00:06:13.105 --> 00:06:14.207
-Jackpot.
-Jackpot.

00:06:14.207 --> 00:06:16.041
-Like jackpot.
-Jackpot.

00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:17.243
-So, it's very important.

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:20.145
So, like, we just want to put
the number, like,

00:06:20.145 --> 00:06:22.014
as our title of the album.

00:06:22.014 --> 00:06:24.750
So, like, that's why.
-The lead single is "On."

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:26.118
-Mm-hmm.
-What does that represent?

00:06:26.118 --> 00:06:29.755
-We've been having
our reboots, so, like,

00:06:29.755 --> 00:06:34.560
our second single was "N.O."
You know what I mean?

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:37.095
So, like, it's a reverse
of "N.O."

00:06:37.095 --> 00:06:38.497
It's like "On."

00:06:38.497 --> 00:06:41.767
And "On" represents, like,
you know, like, "bring it on."

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:46.172
Like, so, we admit our shadows

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:49.308
and, you know, the honors
at the same time.

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:51.710
We could stumble time to time.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:55.347
You know, we've been through
all these paths

00:06:55.347 --> 00:06:57.216
with shadows and lights
at the same time,

00:06:57.216 --> 00:07:00.252
but we admit all of it,
and, you know, bring it on

00:07:00.252 --> 00:07:03.990
and bring the pain and we're
gonna stand it, and -- Yeah.

00:07:03.990 --> 00:07:05.257
-What is it about your music

00:07:05.257 --> 00:07:07.593
that you think fans
are attracted to?

